{"key":"apphy2-mcq-003","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"The transfer increases the total entropy of the system","working":"According to the Second Law of Thermodynamics, spontaneous processes in an isolated system lead to an increase in total entropy. When a quantity of thermal energy Q is transferred from a hot object at temperature T_h to a cold object at temperature T_c (where T_h > T_c), the change in entropy of the hot object is -Q/T_h and the change in entropy of the cold object is +Q/T_c. The total change in entropy is ΔS_total = Q(1/T_c - 1/T_h). Since T_h > T_c, 1/T_c > 1/T_h, meaning ΔS_total > 0. Therefore, the transfer increases the total entropy of the combined system.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":373,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":373,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":469,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":205,"reasoningTokens":264},"totalTokens":842,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":264,"promptTokenCount":373,"candidatesTokenCount":205,"totalTokenCount":842,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":373}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":205}]},"reasoningTokens":264,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4851,"keyed_label":"B"}
