{"key":"apphy2-mcq-003","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"The transfer increases the total entropy of the system","working":"For a spontaneous process, the total entropy of an isolated system must increase. When heat Q flows from a hot object at temperature T_h to a cold object at T_c, the hot object's entropy changes by about -Q/T_h and the cold object's by +Q/T_c. Since T_h > T_c, the total change is ΔS = -Q/T_h + Q/T_c > 0. Thus energy is spontaneously transferred from hot to cold because this direction increases total entropy, in agreement with the second law of thermodynamics.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":429,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":173,"cacheReadTokens":256},"outputTokens":324,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":148,"reasoningTokens":176},"totalTokens":753,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":429,"completion_tokens":324,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":173,"total_tokens":753,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":256},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":176}},"reasoningTokens":176,"cachedInputTokens":256},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3565,"keyed_label":"B"}
