{"key":"apphy2-mcq-026","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"eΔV","working":"By the work-energy theorem, the work done on a charged particle moving through an electric potential difference is W = -qΔV_actual = ΔK. For an electron of charge -e to be accelerated (gain kinetic energy), it must move toward a higher potential, so ΔV_actual = +ΔV where ΔV is the magnitude of the potential difference. Thus, the gained kinetic energy is ΔK = -(-e)(ΔV) = eΔV.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":358,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":358,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":333,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":124,"reasoningTokens":209},"totalTokens":691,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":209,"promptTokenCount":358,"candidatesTokenCount":124,"totalTokenCount":691,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":358}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":124}]},"reasoningTokens":209,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3847,"keyed_label":"A"}
