{"key":"apphy2-mcq-026","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"eΔV","working":"The electron has charge magnitude e. Accelerating from rest, its gain in kinetic energy equals the work done by the electric field. The change in electric potential energy is qΔV = (-e)(ΔV) = -eΔV when the electron moves through a potential difference of magnitude ΔV. By conservation of energy, the kinetic energy gained is the negative of this change: K = eΔV.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":414,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":158,"cacheReadTokens":256},"outputTokens":508,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":116,"reasoningTokens":392},"totalTokens":922,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":414,"completion_tokens":508,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":158,"total_tokens":922,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":256},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":392}},"reasoningTokens":392,"cachedInputTokens":256},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":5495,"keyed_label":"A"}
